# W3a Mechanical Audit — packet-nesting merge (036-deep-loop-innovation)

Tooling note: read-only (`read`/`grep`/`find`/`ls`) only; no git, no shell. Exact file/line counts were obtained with **boundary probes** (a `find`/`grep` at `limit=k` reports `k results limit reached` iff at least `k` entries exist; one probe at `k` and one at `k+1` pins the count), calibrated on scopes with independently known counts.

## Claim 1 — No old paths left in live documents — **CONFIRMED**

- Exhaustive negative search over all `036/**/*.md`, excluding `**/{research,review,review-archive,scratch}/**`, for `system-deep-loop/04[1-9]-|system-deep-loop/050-` returned **exactly 15 lines**, nothing else: `spec.md:162-166` (5, merged-children block) and `timeline.md:125-134` (10, rows 64-73, `path_at_baseline` cells with "(merged 2026-09-20)"). No fourth class exists.
- Run-record total reconstructed by scope decomposition, summed = **432** (exact): 045 root `research/` **87** (probe-pinned: limit 86→msg, 87→msg, 88→clean), `review/` 67, `review-archive/20260914T165140Z` 74, `20260914T231749Z` 80, `007-worktree-removal/research` 5, `014-alignment-review/review` 18; 049 `001-angle-driven-review/review` 78, `014-post-work-review/review` 4; plus **19** in `001-research-inputs-and-architecture/002-deep-loop-effectiveness-and-fanout/research/iterations-modes/iteration-038.md:368-424`. Total 432 + 15 = **447, exactly as claimed**.
- **Classification nuance on those 19 lines**: they are inside a `/research/` path (class a structurally) but match the literal regex only because of a *different* numbering lineage — they reference `.opencode/specs/system-deep-loop/041-deep-research-loop-instrumentation`, `044-deep-loop-locks-state-and-recovery`, `045-deep-loop-fanout-reliability`. They are not old paths of the ten merged packets. No other line was outside the three classes.
- Run records not rewritten: every run-record hit still carries old top-level paths, and a grep for `036-deep-loop-innovation` inside all run dirs of 045 and 049 returned **zero** hits (a rewritten record would show the nested path). The merge's own exception list agrees: "a merge rewrites no run record" (`scratch/merge-041-050/mapping.md` §3).

